---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Signature from '~/components/brand/Signature.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What GRWU is, who it is for, and where its data comes from.">
  <div class="about">
    <h1>About GRWU</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      GRWU is a set of interactive essays on gravitational-wave data analysis. Each one takes a
      single idea, tells the story of how it came to be needed, and lets you move the figures until
      the idea is yours.
    </p>

    <h2>Two ways to read</h2>
    <p>
      Every essay is written to be read as a story, with figures you can drag, scrub and replay.
      Underneath each idea is its <strong>mathematical layer</strong>: the claim, what may be
      assumed, the derivation with the step it turns on, and what it means. Open one where you want
      it, or all of them at once with the control at the top of an essay.
    </p>

    <h2>What the colours mean</h2>
    <p>
      Colour is never decoration here. <span class="term">Amber</span> is the signal, and anything
      observed or measured. Blue-grey is noise, models and schematics. Red is bias and disagreement,
      and it is always labelled. Every figure also says what kind of picture it is: measured, model,
      schematic, or a control whose answer is known in advance.
    </p>

    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p>
      Strain data comes from the{' '}
      <a href="https://gwosc.org/">Gravitational Wave Open Science Center</a>, which publishes data
      from the LIGO, Virgo and KAGRA observatories. It is analysed in your browser.
    </p>

    <Signature ruled />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 7vh, 5rem) var(--gutter) 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .about h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.2rem);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
